  "comments": "The official Kazakhstan Bank&#039;s mint PROOF set 1993 exists, including 2, 5, 10, 20, 50 tyin 1993<br />\r\nmintage: 50.000<br /><br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/569fb104e38de.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/569fb104e38de.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"136\" /></a><br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/569fb10d42f30.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/569fb10d42f30.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"136\" /></a><br /><br />\r\nKrause catalogue, probably by mistake, lists two types of this coin: KM 2 (brass plated zinc) and KM 2a (copper plated zinc). However, the official sources from Kazakhstan, as well as Schön catalogue mention only one type of the coin, made from brass.<br />\r\nSome coins are yellow while others are red. This difference is due to an alteration of the colour of the outside layer of the coin over time.<br />\r\nSee: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2PTojcIGImY\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2PTojcIGImY</a>",
